# Header helper copy → info icon

Do not put long explanatory paragraphs under dialog, page, or section titles.

Put that copy in an info icon **directly to the right of the title** (same row, after the title text). Use the existing title + `Popover` + `Info` pattern in `StatementAiRulesDialog` and `StatementUpload`.

Keep a `sr-only` description when the dialog still needs an accessible description.

Do this for new UI and when editing existing headers with helper text.

## Info icon message formatting

Do not dump one long paragraph into the info popover.

Format helper copy so it scans fast:

1. **Short lead** in `PopoverDescription` (one sentence: what this is / does).
2. **Bullets** when there are 2+ distinct points (loan kinds, steps, caveats, options). Prefer a `<ul className="list-disc …">` sibling under the header, not a wall of text inside the description `<p>`.
3. Keep each bullet to one idea. Skip bullets when a single short sentence is enough (field-level tips).

Example shape:

```tsx
<PopoverHeader>
  <PopoverTitle>Register Lending Account</PopoverTitle>
  <PopoverDescription>Track a loan with amortization terms.</PopoverDescription>
  <ul className="mt-1.5 list-disc space-y-1 pl-4 text-muted-foreground">
    <li>Mortgage, auto, student, personal, HELOC, or other</li>
    <li>Upload a PDF or photo to fill the form from a scan</li>
    <li>OCR stays encrypted for later viewing</li>
  </ul>
</PopoverHeader>
```
